    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (68.51) and **Jonathan Aranda** (67.88) headline our offensive output. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Shane Baz; his projection is boosted by a 10% platoon edge and the added potential for stolen bases, as we specifically track slow pitcher deliveries to optimize our scarcity-driven focus on speed. Meanwhile, **Jonathan Aranda** secures a top-tier score thanks to a soft matchup against Sandy Alcantara (4.42 xERA) and the immense value added by his presumed #2 spot in the order, which provides the volume needed to maximize his strong xwOBA. **Lawrence Butler** (64.46) and **Masyn Winn** (63.37) also grade out as strong starts, with **Masyn Winn** thriving in his leadoff role against Rhett Lowder, further buoying our team\u2019s stolen base ceiling.\n\nConversely, we are forced to treat **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (52.83) with caution. While he is a perennial powerhouse, his matchup against the elite Jacob deGrom suppresses his ceiling, and we are wary of the 40% stolen base prevention rate inherent to facing an ace of that caliber. Our toughest bench decision centered on **Gleyber Torres** (51.01). While **Gleyber Torres** provided a solid floor due to his leadoff positioning, he ultimately fell short of our high-efficiency threshold for the day due to a poor platoon matchup against Luis Castillo. We opted to prioritize **Gavin Sheets** (49.91) in the final utility slot, hoping that his specific platoon advantage against Huascar Brazob\u00e1n yields a more productive outcome than the risk associated with a tough right-on-right matchup for **Gleyber Torres**.\n\nFinal warning: all projections are currently derived from \"Lineup Pending\" statuses. We are monitoring conditions closely, particularly the \"Wind In\" factor impacting **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman** in their matchup against Jameson Taillon. Should official lineups shift these players into lower-value slots, we may see a significant drop in their daily efficiency scores, necessitating a quick pivot to our bench assets like **Geraldo Perdomo** or **Taylor Ward**.",
